.TH RENAMEAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
renameat \- rename entries relative to directory descriptors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int renameat(int " old_directory ", const char* " old_path ","
.BI "             int " new_directory ", const char* " new_path ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Renames or moves an entry, resolving each relative path from its corresponding
open directory descriptor or the current directory for
.BR AT_FDCWD .
An absolute path ignores its corresponding descriptor. Linux replacement and
cross\-filesystem restrictions apply, as with
.BR rename (3crunch).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged, or \-1 on failure with positive Linux
.BR errno .
.SH NOTES
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rename (3crunch),
.BR renameat (2)
